{%- comment %}
  "Request Quote Review" popup for the GymBuild PDP
  (sections/main-product-ab-test-asjads-pdp.liquid only).
  Figma: file XBaAGVhSupd0fvIcXd28qw, node 4145:82852.

  Centered <modal-dialog> (Dawn's custom element, assets/global.js) — same
  open/close/focus-trap/ESC/backdrop-click mechanics as
  gymbuild-customize-popup.liquid's drawer, but centered-dialog CSS instead
  of a right-side drawer. Own class (.gymbuild-quote-review-modal), not
  Dawn's shared .product-popup-modal, for the same reason the customize
  drawer avoided it: that class is still live elsewhere in the theme.

  TWO ENTRY POINTS open this same modal (confirmed 2026-09-02): the main
  PDP's "Request Quote Review" button, and the "Request Quote Review"
  button inside gymbuild-customize-popup.liquid's footer. Both carry
  [data-gymbuild-open-review]; a single shared listener below (a) closes
  the customize drawer if it's open, (b) re-populates the Swaps and
  Customizations summary, the Add-Ons summary, and the price breakdown
  from whatever is currently selected, then (c) shows this modal. This is why the swap cards in that
  other snippet also carry data-original-* attributes (added alongside
  the existing mutable data-item-* ones specifically to support this) —
  comparing original vs. current is how a "swap" is detected here.

  THE SUBTOTAL HAS TWO SOURCES, not one (add-ons added 2026-09-18): the
  swap deltas from the customize drawer's cards, AND whatever is toggled
  on in the PDP's add-ons carousel (product-add-ons-quote.liquid, read via
  [data-addon-state="selected"] / data-addon-price-cents). Both are read
  fresh from the DOM each time this modal opens, never tracked in a
  parallel JS array. Before 2026-09-18 only swaps were counted, so the
  "Estimated equipment subtotal" understated the build whenever any add-on
  was selected. Keep both sources in any future change to this math — the
  customize drawer's own footer subtotal reads the same two sources.

  UI ONLY, per explicit direction (2026-09-08): everything that's already
  real/live is wired dynamically (package name/price/SKU/weight, the live
  swap state and its price deltas, the build page URL). The "Submit
  GymBuild Quote Review" button does nothing on click — no payload is
  assembled, nothing is submitted anywhere. That wiring (and the target
  webhook, e.g. n8n) is future work — see CLAUDE.md's "Data Wiring Notes".

  TWO FIELDS HAD NO REAL DATA SOURCE YET (updated 2026-09-03: hidden from
  customers rather than shown as TODO placeholders, per explicit direction):
  - "Package code" — Figma's "GYMPKG-1500SQFTB" matches no real field on
    this product (checked live: closest are the product_code metafield
    "FF-BYOG" and mpn/vendor_part_no "BYOG-1500", neither matches). The
    whole Details-list line is omitted until a real field exists
    post-metaobjects — don't add it back as a TODO string.
  - "Delivery & Installation Options" — no real option list or tooltip
    copy exists yet (Figma's "Curbside"/"White Glove" labels are
    themselves unapproved copy, not just missing a "TODO:" prefix — see
    CLAUDE.md non-negotiable #7). The <select> is left with only its
    blank "Select your preference" option and the "?" tooltip is
    removed; add the real <option> values/labels once approved, not
    before.

  The disclaimer paragraph ("Equipment subtotal only...") is rendered
  verbatim from Figma and is real customer-facing copy — per CLAUDE.md
  non-negotiable #7, it needs human review before this ever goes live,
  same as any other new customer-facing copy in this build.
{% endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign review_payload_image = current_variant.featured_image
  if review_payload_image == blank
    assign review_payload_image = product.featured_image
  endif
  assign review_payload_image_url = review_payload_image | image_url: width: 520
  assign review_payload_build_url = shop.url | append: current_variant.url
-%}

{% comment %}
  data-review-* below is the machine-readable mirror of the package facts
  displayed in this modal, for the Phase 3 quote-payload builder. The
  visible copy is formatted for humans (money / weight_with_unit), and
  parsing "$70,673.30" or "4284.0 lb" back into numbers is lossy and
  locale-fragile — so every value here is raw: price in cents, weight as a
  plain number plus its unit, URLs absolute. Same convention as
  data-item-* / data-addon-* elsewhere in this build.

  No package code is emitted: no real source field exists for it yet (see
  the header comment above), and the payload builder should send null
  rather than anything invented here.
{% endcomment %}
<modal-dialog
  id="GymBuildQuoteReviewModal-{{ section.id }}"
  class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal"
  data-review-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-review-variant-id="{{ current_variant.id }}"
  data-review-sku="{{ current_variant.sku | escape }}"
  data-review-package-size="{{ current_variant.title | escape }}"
  data-review-base-price="{{ current_variant.price }}"
  data-review-weight="{{ current_variant.weight_in_unit }}"
  data-review-weight-unit="{{ current_variant.weight_unit }}"
  data-review-image="{{ review_payload_image_url }}"
  data-review-build-url="{{ review_payload_build_url }}"
>
  <div
    role="dialog"
    aria-label="Request quote review for this build"
    aria-modal="true"
    class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__content"
    tabindex="-1"
  >
    <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__header">
      <h2 class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__title">Request quote review for this build</h2>
      <button
        type="button"
        id="ModalClose-GymBuildQuoteReview-{{ section.id }}"
        class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
      >
        {% render 'icon-close' %}
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__body">
      <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package">
        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-image-wrap">
          {% if current_variant.featured_image %}
            {%- liquid
              assign review_package_image_alt = current_variant.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape
            -%}
            {{
              current_variant.featured_image
              | image_url: width: 160
              | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: review_package_image_alt, class: 'gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-image'
            }}
          {% elsif product.featured_image %}
            {%- liquid
              assign review_package_image_alt = product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape
            -%}
            {{
              product.featured_image
              | image_url: width: 160
              | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: review_package_image_alt, class: 'gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-image'
            }}
          {% else %}
            {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-image placeholder-svg' }}
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-info">
          <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-title">{{ current_variant.title }} Gym Package</p>
          <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__package-price">{{ current_variant.price | money }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__details">
        <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__section-heading">Details:</p>
        <ul class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__details-list">
          <li>Shopify SKU: {{ current_variant.sku }}</li>
          <li>Total Package Weight: {{ current_variant.weight | weight_with_unit: current_variant.weight_unit }}</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__swaps">
        <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__section-heading">Swaps and Customizations:</p>
        <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__no-swaps" data-gymbuild-review-no-swaps>
          No swaps selected — this build uses the default package inclusions.
        </p>
        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__swaps-list" data-gymbuild-review-swaps></div>
      </div>

      <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__swaps">
        <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__section-heading">Add-Ons:</p>
        <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__no-swaps" data-gymbuild-review-no-addons>
          No add-ons selected.
        </p>
        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__swaps-list" data-gymbuild-review-addons></div>
      </div>

      {% comment %}
        A real form element, so the Phase 3 submit handler gets clean key/value
        pairs from new FormData(form) and the browser does the required /
        type="email" validation natively. It has no action and never
        submits anywhere: the guard listener at the bottom of this snippet
        preventDefault()s every submit, so this can't turn into a page
        navigation or hit any Shopify endpoint. The button itself is still
        disabled — nothing is submitted anywhere yet.
      {% endcomment %}
      <form data-gymbuild-review-form>
        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__delivery">
          <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__section-heading">Delivery info:</p>

          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field-row">
            <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field">
              <label for="GymBuildReviewZip-{{ section.id }}">ZIP code</label>
              <input
                type="text"
                id="GymBuildReviewZip-{{ section.id }}"
                name="zip"
                placeholder="Your ZIP code"
                inputmode="numeric"
                autocomplete="postal-code"
                pattern="[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?"
                maxlength="10"
                title="5-digit ZIP code, optionally ZIP+4 (e.g. 94510 or 94510-1234)"
                required
              >
            </div>
            <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field">
              <label for="GymBuildReviewDelivery-{{ section.id }}">
                Delivery &amp; Installation Options
              </label>
              {% comment %}
                Deliberately NOT required: the real option list is still
                missing (no approved source for it — see the header
                comment), so a required select with only the empty
                placeholder would make the form permanently unsubmittable.
                Add required at the same time the real options are added.
              {% endcomment %}
              <select id="GymBuildReviewDelivery-{{ section.id }}" name="delivery_preference">
                <option value="">Select your preference</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field">
            <label for="GymBuildReviewName-{{ section.id }}">Your name</label>
            <input
              type="text"
              id="GymBuildReviewName-{{ section.id }}"
              name="customer_name"
              placeholder="Name here"
              autocomplete="name"
              required
            >
          </div>

          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field-row">
            <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field">
              <label for="GymBuildReviewPhone-{{ section.id }}">Your phone</label>
              <input
                type="tel"
                id="GymBuildReviewPhone-{{ section.id }}"
                name="customer_phone"
                placeholder="Phone here"
                autocomplete="tel"
                required
              >
            </div>
            <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field">
              <label for="GymBuildReviewEmail-{{ section.id }}">Your email</label>
              <input
                type="email"
                id="GymBuildReviewEmail-{{ section.id }}"
                name="customer_email"
                placeholder="Email here"
                autocomplete="email"
                required
              >
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__field">
            <label for="GymBuildReviewNotes-{{ section.id }}">Notes</label>
            <textarea id="GymBuildReviewNotes-{{ section.id }}" name="notes" rows="3" placeholder="Notes here..."></textarea>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__disclaimer">
          Equipment subtotal only. Final freight, tax, delivery, installation, availability, and approved customization pricing will be confirmed by our team during quote review.
        </p>

        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__breakdown">
          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__breakdown-row">
            <span>Base Package</span>
            <span>{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__breakdown-row" data-gymbuild-review-customizations-row hidden>
            <span>Customizations</span>
            <span data-gymbuild-review-customizations-price></span>
          </div>
          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__breakdown-row" data-gymbuild-review-addons-row hidden>
            <span>Add-Ons</span>
            <span data-gymbuild-review-addons-price></span>
          </div>
          <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__breakdown-row gymbuild-quote-review-modal__breakdown-row--total">
            <span>Estimated equipment subtotal</span>
            <span data-gymbuild-review-subtotal>{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__submit-row">
          {% comment %}
            type="submit" so the browser runs the form's native validation
            once this is enabled in Phase 3 — it stays disabled until then,
            and the form's submit guard below blocks any navigation
            regardless.
          {% endcomment %}
          <button type="submit" class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__submit" disabled>
            Submit GymBuild Quote Review
          </button>
          <span class="gymbuild-quote-review-modal__submit-note">Quote submission unavailable in preview</span>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</modal-dialog>

<style>
